# Maze Game Specification

## Game Overview
A 2D maze navigation game with a 30-second time limit where the player controls a "Labour" character to navigate through a complex maze with many fake paths and touch the helmet at the finish point to win.

## Technical Requirements
- **Framework**: Odyc.js
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Target**: Web browser

## Core Gameplay

### Player Character
- **Name**: Labour
- **Movement**: Grid-based movement
- **Controls**: 
  - W: Move up
  - S: Move down  
  - A: Move left
  - D: Move right

### Timer System - Advanced
- **Duration**: 30 seconds countdown with millisecond precision
- **Trigger**: Starts on first WASD key press
- **Display**: Real-time countdown visible to player with tenths of seconds
- **Timeout**: Shows "No Helmet" message when time expires
- **Auto-Block Controls**: Automatically disable WASD input when timer expires
- **Auto-Show UI**: Automatically display defeat message and restart button on timeout
- **Auto-Show Success**: Automatically display success message and restart button on win
- **Warning States**: Visual/audio warnings at 10s, 5s, and 3s remaining
- **Precision Timing**: Track completion time for performance scoring
- **Speed Bonus**: Award bonus points for faster completion times

### Maze System - Advanced Complexity
- **Generation**: Multi-algorithm hybrid maze with guaranteed solution path
- **Complexity**: Highly complex with BFS distance evaluation between min/max paths
- **Structure**: Grid-based with walls, correct paths, and numerous misleading dead ends
- **Path Width**: All walkable paths are exactly 1x1 unit (single cell width)
- **Fake Paths**: Extensive complex dead-end branches to create maximum confusion (35-50 branches)
- **Start Point**: Fixed entry position at (1,1)
- **Helmet Location**: Fixed at bottom right corner (size-2, size-2)
- **Complexity Evaluation**: Multi-tier BFS analysis to ensure optimal min/max path difference
- **Accessibility**: Helmet position is always reachable from start via pathfinding validation
- **Wall Constraint**: Walls must not appear at the helmet position - helmet must be placed in open path
- **Collision**: Labour cannot move through walls
- **Dynamic Elements**: Moving walls that shift every 10 seconds (optional challenge mode)
- **Trap Cells**: Special cells that temporarily slow movement for 2 seconds
- **Checkpoint System**: Hidden checkpoints that save progress in complex mazes
- **Multi-Level Complexity**: Adaptive difficulty based on player performance history

### Win/Lose Conditions - Advanced Scoring
- **Win**: Labour reaches and touches helmet at finish point within 30 seconds
  - Automatically show success message and restart button
  - Block further WASD input until restart
  - Calculate performance score based on completion time and path efficiency
  - Award bonus points for optimal route discovery
  - Track personal best times and display achievements
- **Lose**: Timer expires before touching helmet
  - Automatically show "No Helmet" message and restart button
  - Block WASD input when timer reaches zero
  - Display performance analytics (distance traveled, time spent)
  - Show heat map of attempted paths for learning
- **Retry**: Button appears automatically after game ends to restart with new complex maze
- **Progressive Difficulty**: Increase maze complexity based on success rate
- **Achievement System**: Unlock special challenges and maze variants
- **Leaderboard**: Track top completion times and optimal path discoveries

## Game Components

### Core Classes (TypeScript) - Advanced Architecture
```typescript
interface Position {
  x: number;
  y: number;
}

interface GameStats {
  completionTime: number;
  pathEfficiency: number;
  totalMoves: number;
  optimalMoves: number;
  score: number;
}

interface Achievement {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description: string;
  unlocked: boolean;
  condition: (stats: GameStats) => boolean;
}

class Timer {
  duration: number = 30;
  remaining: number = 30;
  active: boolean = false;
  precision: number = 100; // millisecond precision
  onExpired: () => void;
  onWarning: (seconds: number) => void;
  start(): void;
  update(): void;
  isExpired(): boolean;
  stop(): void;
  getElapsedTime(): number;
}

class Labour {
  position: Position;
  moveHistory: Position[];
  totalMoves: number;
  isSlowed: boolean;
  slowEndTime: number;
  move(direction: 'up' | 'down' | 'left' | 'right'): void;
  isAtPosition(pos: Position): boolean;
  calculatePathEfficiency(optimalPath: Position[]): number;
  reset(startX: number, startY: number): void;
}

class Maze {
  grid: number[][];
  startPosition: Position;
  helmetPosition: Position;
  trapCells: Position[];
  checkpoints: Position[];
  movingWalls: { pos: Position; direction: Position; nextMove: number }[];
  difficultyLevel: number;
  generate(): void;
  addExtensiveFakePaths(): void;
  evaluateBFSComplexity(): { minDistance: number; maxDistance: number; difference: number };
  validateHelmetAccessibility(): boolean;
  ensureSingleWidthPaths(): void;
  addDynamicElements(): void;
  updateMovingWalls(currentTime: number): void;
  isValidMove(position: Position): boolean;
  isPath(position: Position): boolean;
  isTrapCell(position: Position): boolean;
  isCheckpoint(position: Position): boolean;
}

class Game {
  labour: Labour;
  maze: Maze;
  timer: Timer;
  gameState: 'waiting' | 'playing' | 'won' | 'lost';
  stats: GameStats;
  achievements: Achievement[];
  personalBest: number;
  difficultyLevel: number;
  handleInput(key: string): void;
  checkHelmetTouch(): boolean;
  onTimerExpired(): void;
  blockInput(): void;
  showRetryButton(): void;
  calculateScore(): number;
  updateAchievements(): void;
  showPerformanceAnalytics(): void;
  generateHeatMap(): void;
  adjustDifficulty(): void;
  restart(): void;
  render(): void;
}
```

### Enhanced Maze Generation Requirements - Advanced Algorithms
- **Base Path**: Generate comprehensive path network with single-width corridors using hybrid algorithms
- **Extensive Fake Paths**: Add 35-50 misleading branches of varying lengths (3-15 cells)
- **Path Width Control**: Ensure all walkable paths are exactly 1x1 unit (single cell)
- **Fixed Helmet Placement**: Helmet always at bottom right corner (size-2, size-2)
- **Multi-Tier BFS Complexity**: Analyze min/max path distances with advanced metrics
- **Accessibility Validation**: Verify helmet position is reachable via multiple pathfinding algorithms
- **Wall Placement**: Ensure helmet is placed in open path, walls must not appear at helmet position
- **Complexity Metrics**: Use advanced BFS distance analysis with path efficiency calculations
- **Dynamic Complexity**: Adjust maze difficulty based on player performance history
- **Algorithm Fusion**: Combine Recursive Backtracking, Hunt-and-Kill, and Wilson's algorithms
- **Trap Integration**: Strategically place trap cells to increase navigation complexity
- **Checkpoint Placement**: Add hidden progress save points in longer maze sections
- **Moving Elements**: Implement optional dynamic walls for advanced challenge modes
- **Performance Optimization**: Ensure maze generation completes within 500ms for smooth gameplay

### Input System
- Listen for keydown events
- Map WASD keys to movement directions
- Start timer on first movement
- Validate moves against maze walls
- Update Labour position if valid

### Timer System
- 30-second countdown display
- Starts when first WASD key is pressed
- Updates every second
- Triggers game over when expired

### Game States
- **Waiting**: Before first move, timer not started
- **Playing**: Timer active, player can move
- **Won**: Labour touched helmet within time limit
- **Lost**: Timer expired before touching helmet

### UI Elements
- **Timer Display**: Shows remaining seconds
- **Status Messages**: Game instructions and results
- **Retry Button**: Appears after win/lose to restart game

## Game Flow - Advanced Mechanics
1. Initialize advanced maze generation with hybrid algorithms and performance monitoring
2. Generate multi-tier complexity maze with 35-50 fake dead-end paths for maximum confusion
3. Ensure all paths are exactly 1x1 unit width with advanced collision detection
4. Place helmet at fixed bottom right position (size-2, size-2) with accessibility validation
5. Evaluate multi-dimensional BFS complexity by analyzing min/max path distances and efficiency metrics
6. Validate helmet accessibility using multiple pathfinding algorithms and complexity requirements
7. Add dynamic elements: trap cells, checkpoints, and optional moving walls
8. Place Labour at fixed start position (1,1) and initialize performance tracking
9. Wait for first WASD input to start precision timer with millisecond accuracy
10. Listen for WASD input, move Labour, and track movement history for analytics
11. Update timer countdown display with precision timing and warning states
12. **Automatically check timer expiration and handle timeout with performance analysis**
13. Check if Labour touched helmet at bottom right (win condition with scoring)
14. **Automatically show result message, performance analytics, and retry button on game end**
15. **Block WASD input when game state is 'won' or 'lost' with achievement processing**
16. Calculate performance score, update achievements, and adjust difficulty level
17. Display performance analytics including path efficiency and completion time
18. Allow restart with new complex maze, updated difficulty, and BFS complexity evaluation

- **Visual Elements**
- **Labour**: Distinct character sprite/icon
- **Walls**: Solid barriers that must not appear at helmet position
- **Paths**: Clear walkable areas (both correct and fake)
- **Complex Dead Ends**: Multiple misleading paths of varying lengths
- **Start**: Green marker or distinct starting area
- **Helmet**: Goal object at accessible finish position with no walls
- **Timer**: Countdown display (30, 29, 28...)
- **Victory**: Helmet earned message
- **Defeat**: "No Helmet" message
- **Retry Button**: Restart game option

## Maze Complexity Requirements
- **Minimum Fake Paths**: At least 25-35 dead-end branches for maximum complexity
- **Path Width**: All walkable paths exactly 1x1 unit (single cell width)
- **Path Variation**: Extensive different lengths and directions for fake paths
- **Misleading Routes**: Multiple paths that seem promising but lead nowhere
- **BFS Complexity**: Evaluate min/max path distances to ensure optimal difficulty
- **Solution Obscurity**: True path should be highly obscured by fake routes
- **Fixed Helmet**: Helmet location at bottom right corner (size-2, size-2)
- **Accessibility Guarantee**: Always ensure helmet can be reached from start
- **Complexity Threshold**: BFS distance difference must meet minimum complexity requirements
